==District 2==
{{see also|Michigan's 2nd congressional district}}
The 2nd district is located in [[West Michigan]] and is anchored by the [[Grand Rapids metropolitan area|suburbs of Grand Rapids]] such as [[Kentwood, MI|Kentwood]] and [[Wyoming, MI|Wyoming]], other cities include [[Holland, MI|Holland]] and [[Muskegon, MI|Muskegon]]. This district has a PVI of R+9. The incumbent is Republican [[Bill Huizenga]], who has represented the district since 2011. He was re-elected to a fourth term with 63% of the vote in 2016. 

