==District 5==
{{see also|Michigan's 5th congressional district}}
The 5th district is located along the eastern coast of Michigan, centered on the [[Saginaw, Midland, and Bay City metropolitan area|Tri-Cities region]] of Mid Michigan, such as [[Bay City, MI|Bay City]] and [[Saginaw, MI|Saginaw]], and stretches down into [[Flint, MI|Flint]]. This district has a PVI of D+5. The incumbent is Democrat [[Dan Kildee]], who has represented the district since 2013. He was re-elected to a third term with 61% of the vote in 2016.  Kildee considered running for governor in 2018, but decided to run for re-election instead.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.freep.com/story/news/politics/2017/05/08/us-rep-dan-kildee-forego-race-governor/101455586/|title=U.S. Rep. Dan Kildee will forgo race for governor|work=[[Detroit Free Press]]|last=Gray|first=Kathleen|date=May 8, 2017|accessdate=May 10, 2017}}</ref>

