* Rich Eichholz, businessman and biologist<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.mlive.com/news/kalamazoo/index.ssf/2017/07/democrat_focuses_on_economy_in.html|title=Democrat focuses on economy in 2018 challenge to Fred Upton|work=[[Kalamazoo Gazette]]|last=Barrett|first=Malachi|date=July 20, 2017|accessdate=July 21, 2017}}</ref>
* George Franklin, former [[Kellogg's|Kellogg Company]] executive<ref name=kelloggexec>{{cite web|url=http://www.wsjm.com/2017/03/21/former-kellogg-exec-might-challenge-upton/|title=Former Kellogg Exec Might Seek Upton’s Seat|work=[[WSJM (AM)|WSJM]]|date=March 21, 2017|accessdate=March 23, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.mlive.com/news/kalamazoo/index.ssf/2017/10/former_wmu_trustee_george_fran.html|title=Former Kellogg lobbyist George Franklin announces congressional run|work=[[Kalamazoo Gazette]]|last=Devereaux|first=Brad|date=October 5, 2017|accessdate=October 5, 2017}}</ref>
* Matt Longjohn, physician and former National Health Officer for the [[YMCA]]<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.mlive.com/news/kalamazoo/index.ssf/2017/07/democrat_doctor_challenges_fre.html|title=Democrat doctor challenges Fred Upton in 2018 after health care vote|work=[[Kalamazoo Gazette]]|last=Barrett|first=Malachi|date=July 18, 2017|accessdate=July 18, 2017}}</ref>
;Failed to qualify
* Paul Clements, professor and nominee for this seat in [[United States House of Representatives elections in Michigan, 2014#District 6|2014]] and [[United States House of Representatives elections in Michigan, 2016#District 6|2016]]<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.mlive.com/news/kalamazoo/index.ssf/2017/07/paul_clements_announces_third.html|title=Paul Clements announces third challenge to Fred Upton in 2018|work=[[Kalamazoo Gazette]]|last=Barrett|first=Malachi|date=July 6, 2017|accessdate=July 6, 2017}}</ref><ref name="nictusa.com"/>
