==District 13==
{{main|Michigan's 13th congressional district special election, 2018}}
{{see also|Michigan's 13th congressional district}}
The 13th district is centered on the city of the [[Detroit]] and the immediate surrounding suburbs including [[Dearborn Heights, MI|Dearborn Heights]], [[Garden City, MI|Garden City]], and [[Westland, MI|Westland]]. This is the most Democratic-friendly district with a PVI of D+32. The seat is currently vacant, following the resignation of [[John Conyers]] in December 2017.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Gray|first1=Kathleen|last2=Spangler|first2=Todd|title=John Conyers retires after 53 years in office amid sexual harassment claims|url=https://www.freep.com/story/news/politics/2017/12/05/john-conyers-resignation-detroit-michigan/904737001/|accessdate=December 5, 2017|work=[[Detroit Free Press]]|date=December 5, 2017}}</ref> A special primary and special general election will be held in 2018, on dates coinciding with the already scheduled primary and general elections in a money saving move by [[Michigan Governor]] [[Rick Snyder]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.freep.com/story/news/local/michigan/detroit/2017/12/08/john-conyers-special-election-congress/934206001/|title=Snyder sets Aug. 7, Nov. 6 election dates to replace John Conyers in Congress|publisher=|accessdate=August 29, 2018}}</ref>

Conyers represented the district from 2013 to 2017, and previously represented the 14th district from 1993 to 2013, and the 1st district from 1965 to 1993. He was [[Dean of the United States House of Representatives]], and was re-elected to a twenty-seventh term with 77% of the vote in 2016. 

Former State Representative [[Rashida Tlaib]] won the Democratic primary. Tlaib, however, lost the primary for the special election to Brenda Jones, President of the [[Detroit City Council]]. The winner of the special election will serve for just over eight weeks before the winner of the regular election is sworn in. 

